<GuideLayout
  title="How to Install Minecraft Forge"
  description="Step-by-step guide to installing Minecraft Forge with GDLauncher. Play your favorite Forge mods easily."
  keywords="install forge, minecraft forge, forge mod loader, how to install forge minecraft, forge mods, gdlauncher forge"
  lastUpdated="December 2024"
>
  <h2>What's Forge?</h2>
  <p>
    Forge is the original Minecraft mod loader and still has the biggest library of mods. Most of the classic mods you've heard of (Create, Applied Energistics, Tinkers' Construct) are Forge mods. It's been around since 2011 and isn't going anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Setting up Forge</h2>
  <p>
    Click the <strong>+</strong> button in GDLauncher to create a new instance. Pick your Minecraft version and choose <strong>Forge</strong> as the mod loader. GDLauncher shows available Forge versions for that Minecraft version. The "recommended" one is usually the safest bet.
  </p>
  <p>
    Give it a name and create. GDLauncher downloads Minecraft, Forge, and the right Java version automatically. You're ready to add mods.
  </p>

  <h2>Adding mods</h2>
  <p>
    Open your instance and go to the <strong>Addons</strong> tab. Click <strong>Add Addons</strong> to browse CurseForge and Modrinth together. Search for what you want, click <strong>Download</strong>, and you're set.
  </p>
  <p>
    When looking at mods, make sure they're for Forge (not Fabric) and match your Minecraft version. Most mod pages make this clear.
  </p>

  <h2>Forge vs other loaders</h2>
  <p>
    Forge has the largest mod selection, especially for tech and magic mods. Fabric is lighter and updates faster for new Minecraft versions. NeoForge is a modern Forge fork with active development. Quilt runs most Fabric mods plus some extras.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your choice depends on which mods you want to play. Check if the mod you want is on Forge or Fabric before picking a loader.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p>
    Forge not starting? Make sure you have at least 4GB of RAM allocated (more for modpacks). Try a different Forge version if one specific version has issues. Remove any recently added mods to check for conflicts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mods not working together? Verify all your mods are for the same Minecraft version and the same Forge version. Check mod pages for known incompatibilities or required dependencies. Some mods need library mods to function.
  </p>

  <h2>Popular Forge mods</h2>
  <p>
    Some good starting points: JEI (Just Enough Items) for recipe viewing, Create for mechanical contraptions, Applied Energistics 2 for digital storage, Tinkers' Construct for custom tools, and Biomes O' Plenty for new world generation.
  </p>

</GuideLayout>
